{"ts":"2026-08-25T05:09:03.758Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-5.6-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9b054e739855a3b67742faac","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-5.6-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-6x7o","lineage:pm-96h7","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-a8zm","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-6x7o","lineage:pm-96h7","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Streaming model\n\n- subscriptions/listen is one long-lived POST-response stream with explicit requested notification types and a server-minted subscription identifier.\n- tools, prompts, resources, and resource-subscription changes flow only through the opted-in listen stream.\n- progress and message notifications remain on the response stream of their originating request.\n- A broken request stream loses that in-flight request and the client retries with a new JSON-RPC request id.\n- STDIO and Streamable HTTP share SDK handlers, cancellation, ordering, backpressure, heartbeat policy, and structured failures.\n- Streamable HTTP validates Mcp-Method and Mcp-Name and supports declared x-mcp-header parameter mappings without header injection."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-v7e337"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"MCP subscriptions and transports: subscriptions/listen, request-scoped streams, Streamable HTTP headers, retry semantics, and stdio parity"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Replace connection-session and legacy subscription behavior with the 2026-07-28 long-lived listen request, request-scoped notifications, required headers, and explicit broken-stream retry semantics."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:mcp","cancellation","headers","progress","stdio","streamable-http","streaming","subscriptions"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-25T05:09:03.758Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-25T05:09:03.758Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/deadline","value":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":840},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"subscriptions/listen supports every specified notification type and tags notifications with the negotiated subscription id; Legacy HTTP GET, resources/subscribe, resources/unsubscribe, session headers, Last-Event-ID, SSE event ids, and redelivery semantics are absent from the canonical path; Progress and logging notifications remain request-scoped and cannot leak across concurrent requests; STDIO and Streamable HTTP pass equivalent tool, resource, prompt, cancellation, backpressure, disconnect, and retry cases; Mcp-Method, Mcp-Name, and x-mcp-header behavior is schema-derived, validated, and covered against injection and mismatch"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"Transport parity without protocol sessions"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Provide standards-correct stdio and Streamable HTTP operation for request responses, opted-in changes, progress, cancellation, and disconnect recovery"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Hosts can deploy pm locally or remotely with one transport-neutral state model"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"The revision removes HTTP GET, MCP session IDs, resource subscribe methods, SSE resumability, and Last-Event-ID while adding subscriptions/listen and required POST headers"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-rs9vry"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"critical"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-dj98","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-25T05:09:03.758Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-vae5ec","kind":"blocked_by","created_at":"2026-08-25T05:09:03.758Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-x705zo","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-25T05:09:03.758Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-25T05:09:03.758Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate check evidence: searched all statuses for subscriptions/listen resourceSubscriptions Streamable HTTP Mcp-Session-Id Last-Event-ID Mcp-Method Mcp-Name x-mcp-header and stream retry. No item covers the new transport model."}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"af662e84b4e3b2c44413299711c260ad9e105a2a961c9475f45f2569d6212b88","item_hash_version":2,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
